<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Adaptive launcher icon — used on Android 8.0 (API 26) and above, which
    is the overwhelming majority of devices. Older versions keep falling
    back to the plain mipmap-*/ic_launcher.png files, so both have to stay.

    Why this exists: without an adaptive icon, Android 8+ takes the legacy
    PNG, shrinks it, and drops it on a plain white rounded square of its
    own making. Supplying the layers here means the launcher masks Hops'
    own artwork to whatever shape the device uses (circle, squircle,
    rounded square) instead of boxing it.

    Geometry: the foreground is a 108dp canvas whose inner 72dp is the safe
    zone — anything outside can be cropped by the mask, and the system also
    shifts the layers slightly for parallax. ic_launcher_foreground.png
    therefore draws the bunny at 63% of the canvas, centred, which keeps it
    inside the safe zone with a little margin.

    The background is a flat colour rather than an image: the artwork has a
    transparent background, and a solid fill is what the launcher was
    already compositing behind it.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <!-- Themed icons (Android 13+): the launcher discards colour and tints
         the silhouette to match the wallpaper, so this layer is the same
         geometry flattened to a single tone. Ignored on older versions. -->
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
